IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-part3a-consolidation`

-- je21-tests-part3a-consolidation: tests for Articles 12 to 14.
-- The expected values were written by hand from the text of Articles 12 to 14 and the endnotes (the Law, and so Part 3, in force on 28 September 2021) before the module was run.

§ `Articles 12 to 14 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings`

`L3 default` MEANS `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
`L3 refuse` MEANS `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`

§§ `12 Types of legislation`

#ASSERT `Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) and (4): the text is consolidated legislation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) and (4): the text is consolidated legislation` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 12(3) and (4): the text is consolidated legislation` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 12(1): Part 3 applies in respect of the text` `as-enacted legislation`
#ASSERT `Article 12(1): Part 3 applies in respect of the text` `consolidated legislation`
#ASSERT `Article 12(1): Part 3 applies in respect of the text` `revised legislation`

§§ `13(1) The duty to prepare a consolidated version`

-- Jersey legislation commenced, amended or revised after Part 3 came into force: a consolidated version is required.
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is revised` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
-- Not any of the three events.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `none of these has happened` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
-- Legislation that only amends or commences other legislation, or an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2): excluded.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE TRUE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
-- Not Jersey legislation.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` FALSE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1) `L3 default`
-- The day edges: 27 September 2021 is before Part 3, 28 September 2021 is the day it began, 29 September 2021 after.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 27) `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 27) `L3 refuse`
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 28) `L3 default`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 28) `L3 refuse` BECAUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 3 of the Law came into force, so whether an event that day was after it cannot be answered"
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 29) `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 29) `L3 refuse`

§§ `13(2) The statement a consolidated version carries`

#ASSERT `Article 13(2): the consolidated legislation includes the statement the Law requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 13(2): the consolidated legislation includes the statement the Law requires` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 13(2): the consolidated legislation includes the statement the Law requires` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 13(2) speaks of consolidated legislation, and the text is not consolidated legislation"

§§ `14(1) The editorial changes`

#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the removal of another provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers spent or no longer operative` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of any other errors of a similar nature` TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `changes in punctuation, and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives, to add or remove a provision in a list` TRUE
-- The power is over consolidated legislation.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` FALSE

§§ `14(2) No change has effect to the extent of changing a meaning`

#ASSERT `Article 14(2): the editorial change has effect in full` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(2): the editorial change has effect in full` TRUE

§§ `14(3) Formatting and presentational changes`

#ASSERT `Article 14(3): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the formatting or presentational change` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(3): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the formatting or presentational change` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(3): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the formatting or presentational change` FALSE TRUE

§§ `14(5) Changes that must be set out`

#ASSERT `Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` TRUE TRUE

§§ `14(6) Correcting a published version`

#ASSERT `Article 14(6): the Principal Legislative Drafter may correct the error` `a published version of as-enacted legislation, with an error that occurred after it was made`
#ASSERT `Article 14(6): the Principal Legislative Drafter may correct the error` `a published version of revised legislation, with an error that occurred after its revision`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 14(6): the Principal Legislative Drafter may correct the error` `any other published version or error`
